
  WHAT CAN YOU DO TO AN EIGENVALUE?

======================================================================

  THE EIGENVALUE SPECTRUM AT n=6 (m=10)
  --------------------------------------------------

  lambda_k = (10-2k)/10 = (5-k)/5 for k=0,...,10

  k= 0: lambda =      1 = +1.0000
  k= 1: lambda =    4/5 = +0.8000
  k= 2: lambda =    3/5 = +0.6000
  k= 3: lambda =    2/5 = +0.4000
  k= 4: lambda =    1/5 = +0.2000
  k= 5: lambda =      0 = +0.0000
  k= 6: lambda =   -1/5 = -0.2000
  k= 7: lambda =   -2/5 = -0.4000
  k= 8: lambda =   -3/5 = -0.6000
  k= 9: lambda =   -4/5 = -0.8000
  k=10: lambda =     -1 = -1.0000

  OPERATION 1: LOG (Time)
  --------------------------------------------------

  ln(lambda) = the DECAY RATE of mode k.
  This is TIME: how many steps for this mode to halve.

    k    lambda    ln(lambda)   half-life          nature
    0   +1.0000             0  inf (never)     (permanent)
    1   +0.8000     -0.223144      3.1063  TRANSCENDENTAL
    2   +0.6000     -0.510826      1.3569  TRANSCENDENTAL
    3   +0.4000     -0.916291      0.7565  TRANSCENDENTAL
    4   +0.2000     -1.609438      0.4307  TRANSCENDENTAL
    5   +0.0000          -inf  0 (instant)   (annihilated)
    6   -0.2000     -1.609438+pi*i      0.4307  COMPLEX TRANS.
    7   -0.4000     -0.916291+pi*i      0.7565  COMPLEX TRANS.
    8   -0.6000     -0.510826+pi*i      1.3569  COMPLEX TRANS.
    9   -0.8000     -0.223144+pi*i      3.1063  COMPLEX TRANS.
   10   -1.0000             0  inf (never)     (permanent)

  OPERATION 2: CAYLEY TRANSFORM Q(lambda) = (1+lambda)/(1-lambda)
  --------------------------------------------------

  The Cayley transform maps bounded [-1,1] to unbounded [0, inf].
  It reveals the BOOST STRUCTURE of each eigenvalue.

    k    lambda     Q(lambda)              factored               meaning
    0         1      INFINITY             unbounded        permanent mode
    1       4/5             9                   9/1      3^2 (RAMIFIED^2)
    2       3/5             4                   4/1         2^2 (INERT^2)
    3       2/5           7/3                   7/3  7/3 (FORBID/RAMIFIED)
    4       1/5           3/2                   3/2  3/2 (RAMIFIED/INERT)
    5         0             1                   1/1          1 (IDENTITY)
    6      -1/5           2/3                   2/3  2/3 (INERT/RAMIFIED)
    7      -2/5           3/7                   3/7  3/7 (RAMIFIED/FORBID)
    8      -3/5           1/4                   1/4   1/2^2 (inv INERT^2)
    9      -4/5           1/9                   1/9  1/3^2 (inv RAMIFIED^2)
   10        -1             0           annihilated     fully alternating

  STUNNING DISCOVERY:
  The Cayley transform of the eigenvalue spectrum gives
  9, 4, 7/3, 3/2, 1, 2/3, 3/7, 1/4, 1/9
  = 3^2, 2^2, 7/3, 3/2, 1, 2/3, 3/7, 1/2^2, 1/3^2

  These are ALL expressible in terms of {2, 3, 7} — the HURWITZ PRIMES!
  The Cayley boost spectrum is BUILT from the Hurwitz primes.

  And: Q(lambda_k) * Q(lambda_{m-k}) = 1 for all k.
  The spectrum is SELF-INVERSE under k <-> m-k.
  This is the tournament analog of the FUNCTIONAL EQUATION.

  OPERATION 3: ARCTANH (Rapidity of eigenvalues)
  --------------------------------------------------

  arctanh(lambda) = the RAPIDITY of eigenvalue lambda.
  = (1/2) * ln(Q(lambda)) = (1/2) * ln((1+lambda)/(1-lambda))

    k    lambda     arctanh(lambda)                      simplified
    1       4/5       +1.0986122887                         1*ln(3)
    2       3/5       +0.6931471806                         1*ln(2)
    3       2/5       +0.4236489302          -1/2*ln(3) + 1/2*ln(7)
    4       1/5       +0.2027325541          -1/2*ln(2) + 1/2*ln(3)
    5         0       +0.0000000000                               0
    6      -1/5       -0.2027325541          1/2*ln(2) + -1/2*ln(3)
    7      -2/5       -0.4236489302          1/2*ln(3) + -1/2*ln(7)
    8      -3/5       -0.6931471806                        -1*ln(2)
    9      -4/5       -1.0986122887                        -1*ln(3)

  THE RAPIDITY LATTICE:
  Every eigenvalue rapidity is a rational combination of {ln(2), ln(3), ln(7)}!

  Specifically: arctanh(lambda_k) = (1/2) * ln((10-k)/k)
  For k=1: (1/2)*ln(9) = (1/2)*ln(3^2) = ln(3)
  For k=2: (1/2)*ln(4) = (1/2)*ln(2^2) = ln(2)
  For k=3: (1/2)*ln(7/3) = (1/2)*(ln(7)-ln(3))
  For k=4: (1/2)*ln(3/2) = (1/2)*(ln(3)-ln(2))

  The rapidity lattice is SPANNED by {ln(2), ln(3), ln(7)}.
  By Baker's theorem (1966), these are Q-linearly independent.
  So the lattice is FREE of rank 3, isomorphic to Z^3.

  THIS IS THE SAME RANK-3 STRUCTURE AS THE CUBOID Z/42Z!
  Cuboid:   Z/2Z x Z/3Z x Z/7Z  (finite, mod arithmetic)
  Lattice:  Z*ln(2) + Z*ln(3) + Z*ln(7) (infinite, real line)
  They are the SAME space, viewed through two different completions:
  Cuboid = p-adic view (local, periodic)
  Lattice = archimedean view (global, aperiodic)

  OPERATION 4: ALL OPERATIONS COMPARED
  --------------------------------------------------

    k  lambda          ln         exp         Q     arctanh       1/x       x^2       x^phi
    1   +0.80     -0.2231      2.2255   +9.0000   +1.098612   +1.2500    0.6400   +0.696941
    2   +0.60     -0.5108      1.8221   +4.0000   +0.693147   +1.6667    0.3600   +0.437564
    3   +0.40     -0.9163      1.4918   +2.3333   +0.423649   +2.5000    0.1600   +0.227049
    4   +0.20     -1.6094      1.2214   +1.5000   +0.202733   +5.0000    0.0400   +0.073968
    6   -0.20     -1.6094      0.8187   +0.6667   -0.202733   -5.0000    0.0400   -0.073968
    7   -0.40     -0.9163      0.6703   +0.4286   -0.423649   -2.5000    0.1600   -0.227049
    8   -0.60     -0.5108      0.5488   +0.2500   -0.693147   -1.6667    0.3600   -0.437564
    9   -0.80     -0.2231      0.4493   +0.1111   -1.098612   -1.2500    0.6400   -0.696941

  OPERATION 5: THE SPECTRAL ZETA FUNCTION
  --------------------------------------------------

  Spectral zeta zeta_L(s) = sum_{k=1}^{m} (2k/m)^{-s}

  zeta_L(-2.0) =    15.400000  (RATIONAL)
  zeta_L(-1.0) =    11.000000  (RATIONAL)
  zeta_L(+0.0) =    10.000000  (RATIONAL)
  zeta_L(+0.5) =    11.227293  (ALGEBRAIC)
  zeta_L(+1.0) =    14.644841  (TRANSCENDENTAL)
  zeta_L(+2.0) =    38.744193  (TRANSCENDENTAL)
  zeta_L(+3.0) =   149.691498  (TRANSCENDENTAL)

  Special values:
  zeta_L(-1) = sum mu_k = 11.0 = total connectivity (RATIONAL)
  zeta_L(-2) = sum mu_k^2 = 15.4 = total energy (RATIONAL)
  -zeta_L'(0) = sum ln(mu_k) = -0.989967 = ln(det(L)) (TRANSCENDENTAL)
  det(L) = exp(-0.989967) = 0.371589

  OPERATION 6: THE GOLDEN STEP (lambda^phi)
  --------------------------------------------------

  Evolve the Markov chain for phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2 steps.
  This is the 'most irrational' evolution step.

    k    lambda    lambda^phi     lambda^pi      lambda^e
    1   +0.8000    0.69694147    0.49607600    0.54521937
    2   +0.6000    0.43756360    0.20092853    0.24943223
    3   +0.4000    0.22704897    0.05621272    0.08284893
    4   +0.2000    0.07396781    0.00636973    0.01258933
    6   -0.2000    0.07396781    0.00636973    0.01258933
    7   -0.4000    0.22704897    0.05621272    0.08284893
    8   -0.6000    0.43756360    0.20092853    0.24943223
    9   -0.8000    0.69694147    0.49607600    0.54521937

  All values lambda^phi, lambda^pi, lambda^e are TRANSCENDENTAL.
  (By the Gelfond-Schneider theorem: algebraic^algebraic is
  transcendental when the base is not 0 or 1 and the exponent
  is irrational algebraic.)

  The golden step projects the ENTIRE algebraic spectrum
  into the transcendental world. Nothing survives.

  THE MASTER TABLE: OPERATIONS AND THEIR MEANINGS
  --------------------------------------------------

  OPERATION       WHAT IT COMPUTES           NUMBER FIELD    MEANING
  ---------       -------------------        ------------    -------
  lambda          eigenvalue itself           RATIONAL       STRUCTURE
  ln(lambda)      decay rate                  TRANSCENDENTAL TIME
  exp(lambda)     Boltzmann weight            TRANSCENDENTAL PROBABILITY
  Q(lambda)       Cayley boost                RATIONAL       HURWITZ ENCODING
  arctanh(lambda) rapidity                    TRANSCENDENTAL VELOCITY
  1/lambda        resistance                  RATIONAL       INERTIA
  lambda^2        power                       RATIONAL       ENERGY
  lambda^phi      golden shadow               TRANSCENDENTAL SELF-SIMILARITY
  lambda^pi       circle shadow               TRANSCENDENTAL PERIODICITY
  sum lambda^{-s} spectral zeta               varies         GEOMETRY
  prod lambda     determinant                 RATIONAL       VOLUME
  sum lambda      trace                       RATIONAL       CURVATURE

  THE KEY INSIGHT:
  RATIONAL operations (Q, 1/x, x^2, prod, sum) stay in Q.
  They reveal STATIC structure: Hurwitz primes, energy, volume.

  TRANSCENDENTAL operations (ln, exp, arctanh, x^phi) escape to R.
  They reveal DYNAMIC structure: time, probability, velocity.

  The Cayley transform Q is the LAST rational operation.
  It maps eigenvalues to HURWITZ RATIOS (3^2, 2^2, 7/3, ...).
  Everything after Q (arctanh = ln(Q)/2) is transcendental.

  Q IS THE BOUNDARY BETWEEN COUNTING AND EXPERIENCING.

